Package: survivalGPU
Title: Fast and Scalable Implementations for Survival Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jean", "FEYDY", email = "jean.feydy@inria.fr",role = "aut"),
    person("Alexis", "van STRAATEN", email = "alexis.vanstraaten@outlook.fr", role = "aut"),
    person("Antoine", "Poirot-Bourdain", email = "antoine.poirot.bourdain@gmail.com", role = c("aut","cre")),
    person("Terry", "THERNEAU", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "Author of the 'survival' package, from which the C code and parts of the R code are adapted"),
    person("Pierre", "SABATIER", role = "ctb"),
    person("Anne-Sophie", "JANNOT", role = "ctb"))
Description: Performs survival analysis on graphics processing units
    (GPUs) using Cox proportional hazards and weighted cumulative
    exposure (WCE) models, with support for bootstrap resampling and
    memory management.
    The Cox model is described in Cox (1972)
    <doi:10.1111/j.2517-6161.1972.tb00899.x> and the WCE model in
    Sylvestre and Abrahamowicz (2009) <doi:10.1002/sim.3701>.
    Computations are delegated to 'PyTorch' via 'reticulate'; the WCE
    model additionally requires 'PyKeOps', which is not available
    natively on Windows, but can be used there through the Windows
    Subsystem for Linux ('WSL').
